---
title: "asset config and operation pausing (Current Finance: Asset)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_new: new Asset(interest_model, borrow_config)
    q_new --> q_init_flags: init dynamic fields: all paused = false
    q_init_flags --> q_init_config: store AssetConfig(min_borrow, max_borrow, max_deposit, repay_fee_rate, liquidation_fee_rate)
    q_init_config --> q_active: asset is active

    q_active --> q_change_status: change_operation_status(what, is_paused)
    q_change_status --> q_check_diff: assert current != new value
    q_check_diff --> q_set: set paused flag
    q_set --> q_active

    q_active --> q_flash_trigger: flash_loan_triggered()
    q_flash_trigger --> q_locked: flash_loan_lock = true
    q_locked --> q_flash_finish: flash_loan_finished()
    q_flash_finish --> q_active

    q_active --> q_market_accrue: market.accrue_interest uses repay_fee_rate as reserve_factor
    q_market_accrue --> [*]

    note right of q_init_config
        INV-001: repay_fee_rate is used as reserve_factor in accrue_interest
        INV-002: liquidation_fee_rate is protocol's share of seized collateral
        INV-003: min_borrow_amount prevents dust borrow positions
        INV-004: max_borrow_amount limits total market-wide borrowing per asset
        INV-005: max_deposit_amount limits total deposits per asset
        INV-006: flash_loan_lock is per-asset re-entrancy guard
        INV-007: 5 separate pause flags: borrow, deposit, withdraw, liquidation, flash_loan
    end note
